6. LIQUIDATED DAMAGES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The parties acknowledge that unauthorized distribution or deployment of the
Software causes harm that is real but difficult to quantify precisely, because
it displaces license revenue Licensor would otherwise earn, dilutes the
exclusivity that gives the Software its value, and is impractical to trace
across downstream recipients. The amounts below are the parties' good-faith
pre-estimate of that harm, calculated by reference to Licensor's commercial
usage license fees. They are compensatory, not punitive.

  TIER 1 — UNAUTHORIZED DEPLOYMENT
  Deploying the Software, or a derivative of it, on a property that is not an
  Authorized Property.
      $2,500 per property.

  TIER 2 — UNAUTHORIZED PUBLICATION
  Publishing, mirroring, or otherwise making the Software available to third
  parties, including in a public repository, archive, or file host.
      $10,000 per instance.

  TIER 3 — COMMERCIAL REDISTRIBUTION
  Selling, sublicensing, or distributing the Software as or within a product,
  service, template, theme, or asset library.
      $25,000 per instance, plus disgorgement of all revenue attributable to
      the infringing product or service.

Tiers are not cumulative for a single act; the highest applicable tier governs.
Each distinct property, publication, or product is a separate instance.

These amounts are a floor and an alternative, not a cap. Licensor may instead
elect actual damages, infringer's profits, or statutory damages under the
Copyright Act, and nothing here waives or limits those remedies.

